<p><strong>Welcome to SCP-2212!</strong></p>
<p>This is an SCP puzzle hunt, inspired by such things as the MIT Mystery Hunt and its ilk. You solve puzzles to gradually unlock parts of the main page. There's five puzzles:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/2212-archival-image">Page image</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/2212-archival-class">Object Class</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/2212-archival-containment-procedures">Special Containment Procedures</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/2212-archival-cross-test-log">Cross-test Log</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/2212-archival-interview">Inteview</a></li>
</ul>
<p>These may be solved in any order you like, and are entirely independent of each other. Solving all five will make clear a puzzle in the Description section (don't worry, a much simpler one), and when that's solved, that will unlock the finale, which is in Twine (and not yet quite done, but it should be ready before anyone but a handful of people reach it).</p>
<p>Note that you do not need to know anything about SCP to tackle these. You will need to read some SCPs for the Cross-Test puzzle, but this was written to be approachable even for people unfamiliar with the site.</p>
<p>I would greatly appreciate it if you don't post spoilers in the discussion threads without putting them in a collapsible, like so:</p>
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>[[collapsible]]
The answer is [REDACTED]
[[/collapsible]]</code>
</pre></div>
<p>I will try to answer people's questions, and may adjust puzzles that people are having difficulty with. The answers to the puzzles will not change, so don't worry.</p>

